  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="13de51ad-248d-50a6-9ff4-6884e2ccc231" activityNameId="929546c0-217d-5357-9d28-2e7247ab4c37" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, PVC pipe, DN 300, profile 1</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, PVC pipe, DN 300, profile 1
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: b1e764ef-a00a-4639-ab5b-606258bf49b9
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with PVC-pipe. SN 4-8, DN 300, profile 1 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with PVC-pipe, DN 300, profile 1. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: SN 4-8, DN 300, profile 1 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. PVC-pipe, ID 291-296 mm, outer diameter 315 mm, wall thickness 9-11 mm, 12-15 kg/m, 910-1400 kg/m³. 
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b1e764ef-a00a-4639-ab5b-606258bf49b9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
